# Slice 296 (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM): the book's example (provenance :468-476) -- f has no formal, no visible outer value and
# no established free input x, so `x: j` defines a named Structure x; `return: x` gives no int result and is refused by the
# general rule of the result's check, as for any written Structure returned as int.
fn: f () int
    int: j 3
    x: j
    return: x
end: f
int: code 7
int: v f()
send: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
